    Name a test for each partition
    
    LMSImpl isn't written yet, so every case has to come from the spec.
    Each describe starts with the partitions, then gives a pending test
    (an it() with no function) per case. Each title says the input and
    the expected output, so the suite reads as the list of cases even
    before any assertion exists.
    
    Input partitions come from each parameter's type and @param:
    getLetterGrade has one valid class, 0 to 100, and an invalid class on
    each side of it. Output partitions come from @returns and @throws: the
    five letters and RangeError. The output view is what splits the one
    valid input class into five, and each class gets its two boundaries.
    
    computeGPA has no invalid inputs, but the input view still picks
    cases the output view wouldn't: a 1-credit and a 4-credit course, an
    empty list, a retake. The output view adds 0.0 and 4.0. Retakes go
    both ways, F then A and A then F, so a GPA that counted the best
    attempt instead of the latest would fail.
    
    computeGrade has a precondition: weights must sum to 1. Weights that
    don't aren't a partition. The caller broke the contract, so there's
    nothing to expect.
    
    Each describe also lists what the spec doesn't say: 79.5 or NaN,
    whether "cpsc 310" retakes "CPSC 310", an assessment out of 0. These
    aren't missing tests. They're questions for whoever owns the spec.

